  "result": "Default arg evaluated once, at `def` time. Same list object reused every call that omits `items`. `append` mutates it, so state persists.\n\n```python\n>>> add.__defaults__\n([1, 2],)\n```\n\nFix: use `None` sentinel, build new list per call.\n\n```python\ndef add(x, items=None):\n    if items is None:\n        items = []\n    items.append(x)\n    return items\n```\n\nNow `add(1)` \u2192 `[1]`, `add(2)` \u2192 `[2]`.",
